          "text": "The pattern is indexed by a primitive orthorhombic, ordered-dioxide supercell with approximately\n\n\\[\na=11.555\\ \\text{\u00c5},\\quad b=10.505\\ \\text{\u00c5},\\quad c=9.817\\ \\text{\u00c5}.\n\\]\n\nRepresentative indexing is 15.33\u00b0 (200), 16.87\u00b0 (020), 18.06\u00b0 (002), 22.86\u00b0 (220), 23.77\u00b0 (202), 29.3\u00b0 (222), 30.92\u00b0 (400), 34.12\u00b0 (040), 36.59\u00b0 (004), 46.71\u00b0 (440), and 48.64\u00b0 (404). The extinction pattern is consistent with **Pbca (No. 61), Z = 8**, an ordered, strongly distorted fluorite-related structure.\n\nThe coordinates below are an idealized ordered-fluorite starting model consistent with the cell, symmetry, composition, and dominant diffraction features. The lattice and space-group assignment are more secure than the individual oxygen coordinates; a final publication-quality model would require Rietveld refinement.\n\n```cif\ndata_Hf3SnO8_primary\n_audit_creation_method\n'Powder indexing followed by an idealized ordered-fluorite Pbca starting model'\n_chemical_name_common                 'hafnium tin oxide'\n_chemical_formula_sum                 'Hf3 Sn O8'\n_chemical_formula_structural          'Hf3SnO8'\n_cell_formula_units_Z                 8\n\n_cell_length_a                        11.555\n_cell_length_b                        10.505\n_cell_length_c                         9.817\n_cell_angle_alpha                     90\n_cell_angle_beta                      90\n_cell_angle_gamma                     90\n_cell_volume                          1191.8\n\n_space_group_crystal_system           orthorhombic\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt             'P b c a'\n_space_group_IT_number                61\n\n_diffrn_radiation_type                'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength          1.5406\n_exptl_crystal_density_diffrn         8.72\n\nloop_\n_space_group_symop_id\n_space_group_symop_operation_xyz\n1  'x,y,z'\n2  '-x+1/2,-y,z+1/2'\n3  'x+1/2,-y+1/2,-z'\n4  '-x,y+1/2,-z+1/2'\n5  '-x,-y,-z'\n6  'x+1/2,y,-z+1/2'\n7  '-x+1/2,y+1/2,z'\n8  'x,-y+1/2,z+1/2'\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\n_atom_site_B_iso_or_equiv\nHf1 Hf 8  0.1258  0.1284  0.1209  1.0  0.50\nHf2 Hf 8  0.1264  0.3756  0.3712  1.0  0.50\nHf3 Hf 8  0.3741  0.1231  0.3778  1.0  0.50\nSn1 Sn 8  0.3769  0.3724  0.1263  1.0  0.50\nO1  O  8  0.0540  0.0540  0.0660  1.0  0.80\nO2  O  8  0.0550  0.2000  0.3100  1.0  0.80\nO3  O  8  0.0550  0.3100  0.2000  1.0  0.80\nO4  O  8  0.2000  0.0550  0.3100  1.0  0.80\nO5  O  8  0.2000  0.3100  0.0550  1.0  0.80\nO6  O  8  0.3100  0.0550  0.2000  1.0  0.80\nO7  O  8  0.3100  0.2000  0.0550  1.0  0.80\nO8  O  8  0.2000  0.2000  0.2000  1.0  0.80\n```\n\nThe closely spaced pair at approximately 29.22/29.36\u00b0 could indicate a very small monoclinic distortion or two coherent metric variants. A plausible lower-symmetry survivor is therefore **P2\u2081/c** with approximately the same cell and \\(\\beta\\approx90.4^\\circ\\), but the present pattern does not uniquely establish the corresponding split atomic coordinates. Pbca is the preferred average structure.",
